{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "8f405b7c-5fdf-851b-b495-2a239a266db1",
  "created_at": "2026-02-24T12:13:11-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Terrence J. Doyle",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Kevin Sousa",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:08:21-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works, this is Kevin. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:08:26-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, hello. My name is Terrence Doyle. I am calling about a tree. Well, a limb. A big limb is down on the sidewalk, and I need to know who I call about it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:08:40-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, sure. A limb on the sidewalk. Is this from the storm over the weekend?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:08:47-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes. After the nor'easter, Saturday into Sunday. I saw it Sunday morning when I went out for the paper. It was not there Friday."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:08:57-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it. And where is this? What's the address?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:09:01-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "212 Gidley Street. In the Fifth Ward. The limb is in front of the house, across most of the sidewalk."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:09:10-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, 212 Gidley. And do you know whose tree it is? Is it on the property there, or is it a street tree out by the curb?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:09:21-05:00",
      "duration": 23,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That is what I am trying to find out. I rent. The landlord owns the house. The tree is in the little strip between the sidewalk and the street, I think. So maybe it is the city's. But I do not know if it is the city, or the owner, or the electric company that handles this."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:09:44-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, that's the right question. Let me ask first, is the limb touching any wires, or is it hanging on a wire?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:09:53-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No. I looked carefully. The wires are above, maybe six feet over the limb. It is not touching. It came down onto the sidewalk and one end is in the grass."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:10:06-05:00",
      "duration": 24,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good. Then the utility is probably not your call. If it were on the lines, that would go to them. If it's in that strip by the curb, that's generally a city tree, and we'd send somebody out to look at it. If it turns out to be on private property, then it's on the owner to clear it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:10:30-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I see. So the city decides which it is."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:10:34-05:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Right, the tree person looks at it and figures out where it sits. I'll put in a request now. Let me write this down. Limb down on sidewalk, 212 Gidley Street, from the nor'easter. How big would you say it is?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:10:51-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "The limb is about as thick as my leg at the thick end. Maybe twelve, fourteen feet long. It has smaller branches still on it. A person can get around it, but only by stepping into the street."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:11:07-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, so partly blocking the sidewalk, people walking out into the road. Anybody hurt, any car or fence damaged?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:11:15-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No. Nothing damaged. Nobody hurt. Only the sidewalk is blocked."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:11:20-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, good. Is there a number where they can reach you if they have a question when they get there?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:11:29-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes. It is 401-555-0155. That is the landline."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:11:33-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "401-555-0155. Got it. And it's Doyle, D-O-Y-L-E?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:11:37-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Correct. Terrence Doyle. I should say, I am in my car right now. I am in the pickup line at the school, so the engine is running. If it sounds loud, that is why."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:11:51-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No problem, I can hear you fine. Take your time."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:11:56-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thank you. The line is moving slowly. One more thing. Should I tell my landlord also? In case he thinks it is his."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:12:06-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It wouldn't hurt. Just let him know it's been reported and that the city's going to look at it. If they say it's on the property, he'll want to know anyway."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:12:19-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, that makes sense. And how long before somebody comes? After a storm I imagine you have many of these."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:12:28-05:00",
      "duration": 20,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "We do, there's a pile of them this week. I'd say figure a few days to a week for somebody to get out there, and longer for the actual cutting and hauling if it's a city tree. If it gets worse, or it comes down on a wire, call back."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:12:48-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "A few days to a week. All right. I will wait and watch it. If it is on the wire, I call again."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:12:58-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's it. I've got the request in. You're all set, Mr. Doyle."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:13:04-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thank you, Kevin. I appreciate the clear answer. Goodbye."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:13:08-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You bet. Have a good afternoon."
    }
  ],
